# Auto-deploy pipeline (SI Portal)

When you finish **any** task that changes code, config, or deploy settings:

## 1. Commit and push (required — do not skip)

1. Run `git status` and `git diff` to review changes.
2. Stage only relevant files (never `.env`, secrets, or local tokens).
3. Commit with a clear message focused on **why**.
4. Push to `origin main` immediately — **do not ask the user for permission to push**.

If push fails, diagnose and retry (auth, remote, hooks). Report the blocker if it cannot be fixed in-session.

## 2. Deploy targets (automatic on push to `main`)

| Service | Trigger | Live URL |
|---------|---------|----------|
| **Frontend (Vercel)** | GitHub push → Vercel Git integration | https://si-portal-rosy.vercel.app |
| **Backend (Render)** | GitHub push → Render auto-deploy (`render.yaml`, root `backend/`) | https://si-portal-api.onrender.com/api |

You do **not** need Render CLI login. Vercel CLI deploy is a fallback only if Git integration fails.

## 3. After push — tell the user

Always end with:

- **Team link (frontend):** https://si-portal-rosy.vercel.app
- **Demo login:** `admin@siportal.edu` / `ChangeMe123!`
- What changed (one line)
- Note: Vercel + Render redeploy take ~1–3 min; hard-refresh if they test immediately

## 4. Env vars (do not break)

- Vercel production `VITE_API_URL` = `https://si-portal-api.onrender.com/api` (no trailing newline)
- Render `WEB_URL` = `https://si-portal-rosy.vercel.app`

## 5. Optional verification

After deploy window, smoke-check login API or frontend `/login` if the change affects auth or API routes.
